      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The article describes the features and character of hypertension in certain psychopathological, mainly hypochondriac, states in an endogenous psychic disease. It is shown that the subjective pathopsychological state, the patients' complaints and functional vegetovascular disorders differ from those observed in patients suffering from true vascular diseases. The increase in arterial pressure in the patients studied follows earlier disturbances of the general condition. The dependence of the character of increase in arterial pressure and its tendency to stabilization on the acuity and urgency of senestopathy automatism is noted."},
